values ('a3b4c5d6-7e8f-4a23-8c23-3d4e5f6a7b23', 'acting-iii-period-and-style', 'Acting III (Period and Style)', 'Acting III (Period and Style) trains advanced undergraduate actors to perform heightened language, classical scenes, verse, period behavior, and stylized theatrical worlds with clarity, rigor, embodiment, and imagination. Students develop tools for Shakespeare, Greek tragedy, Restoration comedy, classical monologues, period manners, and style-specific physicality while keeping choices active, ethical, and accessible to contemporary audiences. The course prepares students for advanced acting, classical production work, auditions, dramaturgical collaboration, period/style performance, and capstone productions.');

