ction and Cutting", "children": [{"id": "76669861-6fde-4bff-be77-6a3ab4cd4cad", "type": "concept", "title": "Contrast, length, context, and audition usefulness"}, {"id": "012d0b90-fe7e-447e-b290-93311f560045", "type": "concept", "title": "Clean cuts that preserve argument"}, {"id": "c097d88d-085e-4b05-b1a2-6878f6a535c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding overused pieces unless freshly owned"}], "description": "Students choose material that fits age, range, and training goals."}, {"id": "a827b010-6dec-45ae-89b2-197781369042", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Argument and Journey", "children": [{"id": "6dae7dde-f92e-4af6-9b3c-a37f79494757", "type": "concept", "title": "Opening condition and final condition"}, {"id": "e3b23d5d-9470-4a61-baf1-fc0dfde34fd8", "type": "concept", "title": "Turns, discoveries, and tactical shifts"}, {"id": "5090c17c-8f28-4064-95fd-f88f2736e21c", "type": "concept", "title": "Building to a necessary end"}], "description": "A monologue must change."}, {"id": "e0316e69-1140-4b43-83fa-ad2df23ea1e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Performance Frame", "children": [{"id": "763506a5-e3c2-4745-a80a-928ddc68f77e", "type": "concept", "title": "Slate and setup"}, {"id": "1b20d7b5-82d8-4657-8446-fa1c31822ecc", "type": "concept", "title": "Focus point and imagined partner"}, {"id": "f4545650-4329-47fa-bac4-b81e137ad38d", "type": "concept", "title": "Recovery, pace, and final beat"}], "description": "Students practice presentation skills without losing scene reality."}]}, {"id": "8fa69436-28fc-446a-8b95-fcd26acbba58", "type": "topic", "title": "Performing Classical Scenes", "description": "The final unit asks students to integrate text work, style, voice, body, research, and partner action in performance.", "children": [{"id": "4bcdf784-62db-47a5-9dfc-a783fc09e8d0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integration Rehearsal", "children": [{"id": "82ee7b37-d782-4a80-ac13-56b778d46cfc", "type": "concept", "title": "Text score, movement score, and character stakes"},